cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "splicescope: detecting and characterizing cryptic splicing from splice junctions"
abstract: >-
  splicescope turns splice junctions and a reference annotation into a junction
  taxonomy, model-free splice-site usage (Psi), a count-based differential-splicing
  test, and a prediction of what each cryptic event does to the protein it encodes:
  reading frame, premature termination codon and nonsense-mediated decay. Cassette
  exons and splice-site shifts are both handled. It ships with a Nextflow pipeline,
  a Streamlit dashboard, a real-data validation suite, tests and CI.
type: software
